lines+=['','All twelve static mass/slot relaxations are feasible. The final map\'s unrestricted geometry and mass minimax optimizations hit their 300-second limits; its stricter POD-mask allocation is feasible at 0.420673 and therefore also supplies an unrestricted primal witness. The `≤` entry is this feasible upper bound, not a proved unrestricted optimum. Raw statuses remain unchanged in `packing-summary.json`; `relaxation-status.json` records the subset argument.']
lines+=['', 'POD counts, POD mass and H/M/L mix are retained per map in `summary.json:maps[].pod`; reefer, DG, length counts and each hatch\'s cell/mass caps are in the same rows. All maps have zero movable onboard cargo. Fixed background mass is 2.57–2.70 kt (500), 3.74–3.85 kt (800), and 7.58–8.12 kt (1700), with transverse centre of mass numerically zero. The fixed background cannot be rearranged by the carrier.','', '## Which relaxed limit binds first','', 'The exact geometry CP includes length acceptance, reefer plugs, non-overlapping one/two-cell footprints, and bottom-up support. All twelve solves return OPTIMAL in under one second and pass a separate witness audit. Therefore these basic geometry constraints alone do not explain the wall.','', 'The box/slot LP adds divisible box assignments, fractional bottom-up support, per-stack mass, static allowed DG classes, and explicit on/under-deck requests. Every stack uses the largest of its 20-foot, 40-foot and mixed mass limits: this is deliberately optimistic. The objective minimizes the largest stack mass/cap ratio, so it is a lower bound on necessary local mass utilization, rather than an executable packing. A ratio below one establishes a feasible relaxation only. These LPs omit weight order, composition-dependent mass limits, conditional E6, DG pair segregation/OOG exclusions, visibility, securing and vessel/voyage physics.','', '| Seed | Strict POD mask certificate | Boundary-shared relaxation |','|---|---|---|']
