lines+=['', 'The constructive CP adds actual composition-specific stack mass limits, stack heights and legacy H/M/L order, requires full hold occupancy as a sufficient E6 proposal, and minimizes cargo vertical moment. It omits mixed-length stacking restrictions (including no 20-foot over long boxes and synchronized two-stack support heights), exact kg order, DG pair/OOG interactions and dynamic/physical constraints; it may also overconstrain E6. Therefore neither a CP witness nor CP failure establishes original-map feasibility/infeasibility. Saved witnesses are candidate preferred slots for native replay. Lower cargo KG can raise GM and securing accelerations, so the scalar objective is not a physics guarantee.','', '## Recommendation and verification','', 'Preserve the checker and the fixed train cohort. Investigate completion-aware local packing and alternative layouts before interpreting longer search failure as physical impossibility. Use full physical checking on several complete, balanced low-KG candidates, because relaxed aggregate capacity has substantial room. Treat fore/aft port blocks as a move objective with capacity/mass fallback, not a requirement imposed before proving a feasible packing. Requalify the outward C2 policy through its owning workflow before using it for rejection or per-limit claims.','', f"Evidence: `summary.json` (12-map static/geometry census), `inventory-extra.json`, `packing-summary.json` ({len(p['maps'])}/12 map LP groups complete), map-level `*-packing.json` and sparse `*-packing-witness.npz`, and `geometry.json` witnesses. `binding.json` pins cohort and runtime; the immutable source snapshot identity is `15e3d6ba159dee5b015ad22f67a2191664caec65fe4291136c95124cb9540f44`. Run commands are the three Python scripts in this folder, each with numerical worker counts forced to one. `construct_cp.py` waits for packing completion. No original-map infeasibility certificate exists."]
