lines+=['','## Reproduction and artifact checks','','Worker entry points, from repository root: `.venv/bin/python experiments/mvp/strategy/medium-wall/capacity/analyze.py`, then `packing_lp.py`, then `construct_cp.py` at the same path. The scripts force one numerical/CP worker and retain per-map/per-mode artifacts for resume. The CP controller also waits for packing completion. Never run those three solver entry points concurrently.','','Derived tables are regenerated in this order: `inventory_extra.py`, `background_inventory.py`, `augment_inventory.py`, `table.py`, `hatch_tightness.py`, `relaxation_status.py`, `render.py`, `verify.py`, `complete.py`. `complete.py` requires both CP outcomes. All are in this capacity folder. The primary verification independently checks all twelve input/audit hashes, all 517 immutable runtime files, twelve integer geometry witnesses, 42 feasible LP sparse-matrix witnesses and four strict-mask certificates. Maximum saved LP inequality residual is 6.86e-8 kg and assignment residual 1.25e-11. The two LP optimization deadlines remain labelled unknown; a narrower feasible witness supplies their feasibility implication.','','`cp-summary.json` suppresses unset UNKNOWN objectives and reconciles actual CP plus all search-arm wall times against the chosen one-hour cap for each 121-box map. `completion.json` pins final scripts and key artifacts. The capacity-relaxation evidence is not a full-checker plan certificate. No original-map infeasibility certificate is produced.']
